["Pages/Page_158289652.html","1 Introduction",
"\t\t\n1 Introduction\nObjectives and Content\nThis document describes how to use the logo when using amiibo, the screen images when touching the amiibo to the controller, and how to use sound effects.\nIntended Audience\nThis documentation is intended for planners and application developers.\nWhen to Read This Document\nRead this documentation when you are planning or developing applications.\nFile List\nThis package has the following structure.\nNote: Not all of the files are listed.\n \tFolder Name \tFilename \tDescription\n \t logo\n \t amiibo_logo_application_ver2.ai\n \t amiibo logo data.\n \t\n \t amiibo_icon_application_ver2.ai\n \t amiibo icon data.\n \t\n \t amiibo_settingicon_application_ver2.ai\n \t amiibo Settings icon data.\n \t\n \t amiibo_nfc_area_mark_application_ver2.ai\n \t NFC touchpoint data.\n \t image\n \tamiibo_Message_YYYYMMDD.xlsx \t List of text data in various languages for the amiibo touchpoint locator image.\n YYYYMMDD indicates the year, month, and day of the file version.\n \t\n \ttouch_guide_image-NX_JOY-CON_720.psd \t720p amiibo touchpoint locator image (for Joy-Con).\n \t\n \ttouch_guide_image-NX_Pro_Controller_720.psd \t720p amiibo touchpoint locator image (for Nintendo Switch Pro Controller).\n \t\n \ttouch_guide_image-NX-Joy-Con_Pro_Controller_720.psd \t720p amiibo touchpoint locator image (for Joy-Con and Nintendo Switch Pro Controller).\n \t\n \ttouch_guide_image-NX_JOY-CON_1080.psd \t1080p amiibo touchpoint locator image (for Joy-Con).\n \t\n \ttouch_guide_image-NX_Pro_Controller_1080.psd \t1080p amiibo touchpoint locator image (for Nintendo Switch Pro Controller).\n \t\n \ttouch_guide_image-NX-Joy-Con_Pro_Controller_1080.psd \t1080p amiibo touchpoint locator image (for Joy-Con and Nintendo Switch Pro Controller).\n \t\n \t touch_guide_image-3DS-ja.psd\n \t amiibo touchpoint locator image (for 3DS) (JP).\n \t\n \t touch_guide_image-3DS-en.psd\n \t amiibo touchpoint locator image (for 3DS) (EN).\n \t\n \t touch_guide_image-New3DS_3DS-ja.psd\n \t amiibo touchpoint locator image (for New 3DS/3DS) (JP).\n \t\n \t touch_guide_image-New3DS_3DS-en.psd\n \t amiibo touchpoint locator image (for New 3DS/3DS) (EN).\n \t\n \t touch_guide_image-New3DS-ja.psd\n \t amiibo touchpoint locator image (for New 3DS) (JP).\n \t\n \t touch_guide_image-New3DS-en.psd\n \t amiibo touchpoint locator image (for New 3DS) (EN).\n \t se\n \t amiibo_se_success.wav\n \t Sound effect when starting loading and writing.\n \t\n \t amiibo_se_error.wav\n \t Sound effect for errors.\nCONFIDENTIAL\n",0,"en-US"]
,["Pages/Page_161297893.html","3 NFC Touchpoint Icon",
"\t\t\n3 NFC Touchpoint Icon\nThis section contains guidelines and considerations for using the NFC touchpoint icon.\nIntended Uses\nIf the amiibo must come into contact with the New Nintendo 3DS, display the NFC touchpoint on the lower screen of the New Nintendo 3DS.\nMinimum Margin\nThe NFC touchpoint must be surrounded by a minimum margin. As a general rule, this margin may not contain images or text.\nThe minimum margin may be compromised when the display space is limited.\nThe minimum margin is included in the distributed data as a clear rectangle. See the resource for details.\nMinimum Margin (Red Line)\n Color, Background Color, and Effects\nThere are no specifications for the color or background color of the NFC touchpoint except that it must be visible.\nAny colors may be used.\n Notes\n You can add a drop shadow or outer glow effect to ensure visibility.\nA text outline is generally prohibited.\nCONFIDENTIAL\n",0,"en-US"]
,["Pages/Page_161297947.html","4 Touchpoint Locator Image",
"\t\t\n4 Touchpoint Locator Image\nThis screen helps guide the user to the proper tap position for amiibo for Nintendo Switch™ (hereafter \"Switch\") and the Nintendo 3DS family.\nRules for Using Artwork\nAlthough the artwork included in this package can be used as is for purposes such as Nintendo Switch and Nintendo 3DS family applications and related printed materials, the composition of colors and lines in this artwork can also be tailored to fit the brand concept and look of each game.\nThe following are examples of such alterations.\n \tChanging to more appropriate colors, or adding patterns\n \tAdding shadows, glow effects, textures, or borders as needed\n \tSimplifying the artwork by using just its outline, or removing the outline entirely\n \tChanging to a more digital or hand-drawn feel\nHowever, you must ensure that such arrangements do not confuse users.\nThe following are examples of arrangements that could confuse users.\n \tThe artwork is arranged in a way that causes the user to misjudge the size of the product.\nExample) The Joy-Con appear larger than the Nintendo Switch Pro Controller when they are both shown together in the same space. (Obviously, the Joy-Con are smaller.)\n \tMaking a product appear as a different one by removing or changing the elements that are unique to that product, making it hard to understand what the drawing represents.\nOne example would be removing the rails from the Switch main unit and the Joy-Con controllers to make it resemble a Wii U GamePad.\nIllustrations are available in both the RGB and CMYK color modes. Use the RGB versions when working with applications or websites. Use the CMYK version when working with printed materials.\n Note\n If anything about using or arranging the illustrations is unclear, or if you want to use a particular effect, contact your Nintendo representative.\nAnnouncement Messages in Various Languages\nAnnouncement messages in various languages are compiled in amiibo_Message_YYYYMMDD.xlsx in the image folder. YYYYMMDD indicates the year, month, and day representing the file version.\nLanguages for Provided Announcement Messages\n \tJapanese, US English, Canadian French, Latin American Spanish, UK English, EU French, EU Spanish, German, Italian, Dutch, Russian, Portuguese, Korean, Traditional Chinese, Simplified Chinese.\nText layers for the various languages are provided in the PSD file for Switch images only. For the Nintendo 3DS family, Japanese and English PSD files are provided.\nFor Switch\nThese images are for the Joy-Con™, Nintendo Switch Pro Controller, and both the Joy-Con and Nintendo Switch Pro Controller.\nThey are used for the Switch LCD screen or TV display.\n Info\n \tUse the touchpoint locator image suitable for the connected controller. Although it is possible to show multi-use indicators for the Joy-Con controllers and Nintendo Switch Pro Controllers, we recommend showing the image for either the Joy-Con or the Nintendo Switch Pro Controller based on which controller is connected.\n \tThe position of the lit player LED can be changed by switching the layer. In the application, use the images where the appropriate player LEDs are lit according to the number of the controller to which the amiibo is loaded.\n \tAlthough it is possible to use images with all player LEDs turned off, we recommend that you use images without turning the player LEDs off.\nJoy-Con\n \t\n \t \ttouch_guide_image-NX_JOY-CON_720.psd\n \ttouch_guide_image-NX_JOY-CON_1080.psd\n There are files for 720p and 1080p.\n Text layers for the various languages are provided.\n JPja: Japanese, USen: US English, USfr: Canadian French, USes: Latin American Spanish, EUen: UK English, EUfr: EU French, EUes: EU Spanish, EUde: German, EUit: Italian, EUnl: Dutch, EUru: Russian, EUpt: Portuguese, KRko: Korean, CHzh: Traditional Chinese, TWzh: Simplified Chinese.\n The display font is not publicly available. If an error indicating that the font cannot be found is displayed, use the outlined layer Text (Outline).\n \t\n \t\n Nintendo Switch Pro Controller\n \t\n \t \ttouch_guide_image-NX_Pro_Controller_720.psd\n \ttouch_guide_image-NX_Pro_Controller_1080.psd\n There are files for 720p and 1080p.\n Text layers for the various languages are provided.\n JPja: Japanese, USen: US English, USfr: Canadian French, USes: Latin American Spanish, EUen: UK English, EUfr: EU French, EUes: EU Spanish, EUde: German, EUit: Italian, EUnl: Dutch, EUru: Russian, EUpt: Portuguese, KRko: Korean, CHzh: Traditional Chinese, TWzh: Simplified Chinese.\n The display font is not publicly available. If an error indicating that the font cannot be found is displayed, use the outlined layer Text (Outline).\n Joy-Con/Nintendo Switch Pro Controller\n \t\n \t \ttouch_guide_image-NX-Joy-Con_Pro_Controller_720.psd\n \ttouch_guide_image-NX-Joy-Con_Pro_Controller_1080.psd\n There are files for 720p and 1080p.\n Text layers for the various languages are provided.\n JPja: Japanese, USen: US English, USfr: Canadian French, USes: Latin American Spanish, EUen: UK English, EUfr: EU French, EUes: EU Spanish, EUde: German, EUit: Italian, EUnl: Dutch, EUru: Russian, EUpt: Portuguese, KRko: Korean, CHzh: Traditional Chinese, TWzh: Simplified Chinese.\n The display font is not publicly available. If an error indicating that the font cannot be found is displayed, use the outlined layer Text (Outline).\nFor the Nintendo 3DS Family\nThese images are for the New Nintendo 3DS system, the Nintendo 3DS system, and both the New Nintendo 3DS and Nintendo 3DS systems.\nFor the New Nintendo 3DS System\n \t\n \t touch_guide_image-New3DS-ja.psd\n \t\n \t touch_guide_image-New3DS-en.psd\nFor the Nintendo 3DS System\n \t\n \t touch_guide_image-3DS-ja.psd\n \t\n \t touch_guide_image-3DS-en.psd\n For Both the New Nintendo 3DS and Nintendo 3DS Systems\n \t\n \t touch_guide_image-New3DS_3DS-ja.psd\n \t\n \t touch_guide_image-New3DS_3DS-en.psd\nHow to Use\nUse these images for screens that describe how to use the amiibo, or to display on the screen when detecting amiibo.\n The image for the Nintendo 3DS Family is made to be displayed on the upper screen, but by trimming the left and right, it can also be used for the lower screen.\nCONFIDENTIAL\n",0,"en-US"]
,["Pages/Page_161298795.html","5 Sound Effects",
"\t\t\n5 Sound Effects\nThese sound effects can be used for amiibo-compatible applications.\nThe following two types of sound effects are available.\n \tWhen starting loading or writing (amiibo_se_success.wav)\n \tError (amiibo_se_error.wav)\n Info\n The use of sound effects is encouraged.\n Basic Sound Effect Operations\nLoad\n Write\n Example Use in amiibo Settings\n Load\nWrite\n Considerations\nSet appropriate volumes for each application.\nCONFIDENTIAL\n",0,"en-US"]
,["Pages/Page_163418625.html","2 Logos and Icons",
"\t\t\n2 Logos and Icons\nThis section contains guidelines and considerations for using the amiibo logo or icons in an application.\nContact your Nintendo representative if anything about these guidelines is unclear, or if you want to use a particular effect.\namiibo Logo\namiibo Icon\namiibo Settings Icon\n Note: For the Nintendo 3DS family and Wii U only.\nAcceptable Uses\n \tUse the amiibo logo and icons to represent amiibo, and in UI elements that jump to amiibo-related features.\n \tUse the logo whenever possible. Only use the icon when use of the logo is impossible due to space restrictions or when you want to match the effects of other UI elements.\n \tUse the amiibo Settings icon for UI elements that take the user directly to amiibo Settings from the application.\n \tWhen using the amiibo icon and the amiibo Settings icon, add descriptive text.\nAlways use text that includes the word \"amiibo\" alongside the icon to clearly indicate that it is related to amiibo.\nWhen writing \"amiibo\" in text, always write the entire word in lowercase.\nHowever, if it is not possible to add descriptive text due to the space limitations, you can use the icon independently without any descriptive text.\nMinimum Margin\nThe amiibo logo is to be surrounded by a minimum margin. As a general rule, this margin area may not contain images or text.\nThe minimum margin may be compromised when the display space is limited.\nThe minimum margin is included in the distributed data as a clear rectangle. See the resource for details.\nMinimum Margin (Red Line)\nSpecified Colors\n Note\n Use one of the specified colors unless it impairs visibility or there is some kind of technical limitation.\nUse an achromatic logo only if none of the specified colors can be used.\nBackground and Effects\nThe primary background color is white and the secondary is black.\nEnsure that visibility of the logo is maintained when you place it on a background color other than white or black.\nYou can add a drop shadow or outer glow effect to ensure visibility.\nA text outline is generally prohibited.\nCONFIDENTIAL\n",0,"en-US"]
